Don't worry, the luck/loadstones are so easy to tell apart:
spoiler follows:
















































When you find a gray stone, kick it.  A luckstone will move like other rocks/gems,
a loadstone is too heavy and you'll get "thump" or perhaps "ouch!" and the stone
won't move.
You may have to dig around the stone if it is located in the end of a corridor.
Once you find a luckstone, identify or #name it.  After that, all gray stones
are loadstones.


